---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const description =
  'Terms and conditions for using elysetindall.com, including portfolio materials, inquiry forms, and paid private voice lessons processed by Stripe.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms" description={description} hideFooterCta>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gel">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-5xl text-spotlight md:text-6xl">Terms &amp; conditions</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
      Rules for using {site.name}’s website ({site.url.replace(/^https:\/\//, '')}). By using this
      site, you agree to these terms. Last updated August 22, 2026.
    </p>

    <div class="prose-site mt-12">
      <h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance</h2>
      <p>
        If you do not agree, please do not use the site. We may update these terms; the version
        posted here is the current one. Continued use after changes means you accept the updated
        terms.
      </p>

      <h2 id="site-purpose">Site purpose</h2>
      <p>
        This website presents {site.name}’s work as a musical theatre actress and vocal coach, and
        provides ways to request casting materials or inquire about private <strong
          >voice lessons</strong
        > (vocal pedagogy, vocal health, and contemporary commercial music). The site does not
        offer acting lessons, monologue coaching, or scene study as advertised services.
      </p>

      <h2 id="content">Portfolio content</h2>
      <p>
        Photos, video, copy, resume materials, and other content on this site are owned by{' '}
        {site.name} or used with permission. You may view them for casting, booking, or personal
        interest. You may not copy, redistribute, train AI systems on, or commercially reuse site
        content without prior written permission, except for ordinary casting/review use of
        downloadable materials provided for that purpose (for example a resume PDF or headshot
        offered on the Materials page).
      </p>

      <h2 id="inquiries">Inquiry forms &amp; contact</h2>
      <p>
        Casting and lesson forms are for genuine professional or lesson inquiries. Do not submit
        spam, abusive content, or false information. Submitting a form does not create a booking,
        engagement, or employment relationship. Availability and a lesson time are confirmed by
        email (or another agreed channel) before a session. Rates on /lessons/book are current
        session fees for private voice lessons; payment terms for prepaid sessions are in{' '}
        <a href="#paid-lessons">Paid voice lessons</a> below.
      </p>
      <p>
        How we handle personal information is described in the{' '}
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, including{' '}
        <a href="/privacy#sms">SMS notifications</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="lessons">Voice lessons</h2>
      <p>
        Lesson inquiries may lead to private voice instruction (vocal pedagogy, vocal health, and
        contemporary commercial music). The site does not offer acting lessons, monologue coaching,
        or scene study. Nothing on this site is medical advice; voice work is educational and
        artistic in nature.
      </p>

      <h2 id="paid-lessons">Paid voice lessons</h2>
      <p>
        When payment is offered on this site, it is for a scheduled (or about-to-start) private
        voice lesson at the published 30-minute or 60-minute rate. Paying does not by itself lock a
        calendar slot until {site.name} confirms the time. Pay the length that matches the session
        you booked.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Processor.</strong> Payments are processed by Stripe. You also agree to Stripe’s
        terms when you complete checkout. This site never asks you to type a card number into a form
        we host.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Cancellation &amp; refunds.</strong> Cancel at least 24 hours before the confirmed
        start time for a full refund to the original payment method. Cancellations inside 24 hours,
        no-shows, and sessions cut short by late arrival may be non-refundable. {site.name} may
        still issue a full or partial refund (for example weather, illness, or a studio
        cancellation) via Stripe. Refund timing depends on the original payment method. Processing
        fees charged by Stripe are typically not returned on refunds.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Disputes.</strong> Contact the studio first so we can refund or reschedule when
        that’s the right fix. Chargebacks may incur Stripe’s dispute fee; keep your confirmation
        emails.
      </p>

      <h2 id="third-parties">Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        The site may use third-party providers for hosting, form verification, email, SMS,
        analytics, and payment processing (Stripe). Links to Instagram, YouTube, or other sites are
        provided for convenience; we are not responsible for their content or policies.
      </p>

      <h2 id="disclaimers">Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided “as is.” We strive for accuracy but do not warrant that content is
        complete, current, or uninterrupted. To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.name} is
        not liable for indirect or consequential damages arising from use of the site. For claims
        about a paid voice lesson, liability is limited to the amount you paid for that lesson. For
        other claims relating to the website itself, our total liability is limited to the greater
        of zero (for free site use) or amounts you paid specifically for website-related services in
        the three months before the claim (if any).
      </p>

      <h2 id="indemnity">Indemnity</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold {site.name} harmless from claims arising out of your misuse
        of the site or violation of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 id="governing-law">Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of New York, without regard to conflict of
        law rules. Courts located in New York County, New York are the exclusive venue for disputes
        arising from these terms or use of the site, except where prohibited by law.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms:{' '}
        <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
        {' · '}
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(.prose-site h2) {
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }
</style>
